/*
 * Template for rofi's palette, rendered by noctalia into
 * ~/.config/rofi/colors.rasi every time the wallpaper or colour scheme
 * changes. Declared in configs/rofi.nix; do not edit the rendered file.
 *
 * This mirrors how HyDE does it. HyDE's wallbash reads
 * .local/share/wallbash/always/rasi.dcol, a rasi body whose colours are
 * `<wallbash_pry1>` placeholders with a literal hex alpha byte appended, and
 * writes the result to a cache path that the rofi themes import. noctalia's
 * template processor is the same idea with double-brace placeholders, so the
 * alpha bytes below are appended the same way.
 *
 * The processor scans comments too, so do not write an example placeholder in
 * this header; a malformed one fails the whole render and nothing is written.
 *
 * Alpha bytes: CC = 80%, D9 = 85%, E6 = 90%.
 *
 * These sit on a blurred wallpaper, since niri blurs behind rofi's layer
 * surface (configs/theming/niri.nix).
 *
 * The three surfaces climb the tonal ramp rather than sitting at the bottom of
 * it, and each is a step more opaque than the one under it: window, then the
 * list card on top of it, then the mode circles on top of that. Reading down
 * the ramp instead (surface_container_lowest for the list, surface_variant for
 * the circles) put the list at #0a1014 and left the circles a hair off the
 * window behind them, so the list swallowed the blur and the rail all but
 * vanished. Lightness is what separates these layers; alpha only decides how
 * much wallpaper shows through.
 *
 * Selection and border take tertiary, not primary. noctalia paints its own
 * highlights (selected clipboard row, active workspace pill) with mTertiary,
 * so primary would leave the launcher accented differently from the bar it
 * opens under.
 */

* {
    main-bg:     #{{colors.surface.default.hex_stripped}}CC;
    main-fg:     {{colors.on_surface.default.hex}};
    main-br:     {{colors.tertiary.default.hex}};
    list-bg:     #{{colors.surface_container_high.default.hex_stripped}}D9;
    select-bg:   {{colors.tertiary.default.hex}};
    select-fg:   {{colors.on_tertiary.default.hex}};
    button-bg:   #{{colors.surface_container_highest.default.hex_stripped}}E6;
    button-fg:   {{colors.on_surface.default.hex}};
}
